WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.201
I wanted to ask you, Mrs.

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.202
Obama, you know,

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:04.904
so many women struggle with self-doubt,

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.073
do you?

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.742
And if you do.

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:11.411
How do you push past it?

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:12.879
Mm hmm.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.647
I talk about this all the time,

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:15.749
especially with

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:16.483
the young girls

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:16.916
I meet,

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.184
because they look at people

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.652
like us in these positions.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:20.954
And they think, well,

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:23.623
you must have been born into that place,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.558
which is the 11 of the reasons

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.360
why when I meet with young girls,

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.895
I don't care where in the world it is.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:29.963
I don't want them to know.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:32.098
Michelle Obama, the former first lady.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:32.966
I want them to know.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.267
Michelle Obama, that girl

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.236
from the Southside of Chicago.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:37.604
I want to break down that

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.839
that wall of impossibility

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.975
to let them know that I am them

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.343
and they are me.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:44.677
And yes,

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:47.080
every other moment I feel self-doubt

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.050
because when you and Sissi

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:50.984
he intentionally

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.619
does that to women and girls,

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.721
it starts at a very early age.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.022
We are.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.491
We question our value, our worth.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.794
We question how we look how we talk,

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:01.995
where we're from.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.831
They are people with power

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.433
who want us to stay small.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.701
They want us to stay doubtful.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.204
And so our cultures reinforce that.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.039
So the one thing I want

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.541
young girls to understand

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.342
is that those feelings are real.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.610
They are not crazy.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.045
They are they

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:22.015
they are indoctrinated in us all.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.818
And we carry them around with us

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.352
our entire lives.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:26.986
And I don't care

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.354
how far you go,

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.390
whether you go to the White House,

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.593
you are constantly batting away.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.061
Those negative messages

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.930
are being not enough.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:37.530
And yes,

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.532
I deal with that to

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.434
and I don't want young women,

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.503
young girls to get ahead of themselves

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:46.406
to think that they have to fix it all now

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.476
in order to break the cycles

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:50.710
of negativity,

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.045
you got to get up every day

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:54.314
and do the work right before you.

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:56.649
That means getting your education

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.185
when the opportunity presents itself.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:01.387
And then focusing on that,

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.423
doing the work, doing your homework,

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.592
getting to the next stage in life.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:06.993
Because if you take

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.062
those small steps over time,

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:11.965
you build up a lifetime of another story

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:12.932
for yourself.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.634
No one can do that for you.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.169
You have to look over your life.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.003
And we as women

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.004
sometimes feel like

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.373
we have to have done everything right

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.975
before we can take credit for

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.309
the things that we have done.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.012
But there is power and

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.313
what we do every day.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.282
And I have to remind myself of that

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.251
every single moment.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.785
But now that I'm older,

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:36.022
I can now look back and say, yeah,

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.590
I am worthy.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.859
I have value,

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.228
but is not because I'm sitting here.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.296
I had that value

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:44.230
when I was three,

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.098
when I was five,

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:47.367
when I was seven, when I was 12.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.868
And for the young girls out there,

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:49.969
you have it now

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.271
you just have to take the time

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.572
to realize it

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:54.140
and be patient with yourself

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:54.807
as you do it.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.210
Because the process takes a lifetime

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:01.447
takes a lifetime.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.951
I am trippin right now that you just said

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.518
that you deal

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.920
with self-doubt all the time,

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.121
like somehow that didn't

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.489
seem to right in the back.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.257
Write back there. Me too.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.025
Right back there

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:13.726
I was like, Don't trip, don't follow

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:15.395
me.

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:16.262
Don't I?

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.231
The same the same things

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.165
Amal and I were like,

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.366
What are you wearing?

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.834
Is this color right?

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.303
Well, this be stupid

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:25.071
to be doing this work with you and also,

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.372
what are you wearing?

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.408
So what do you do, Amal,

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:31.344
when self-doubt attacks you?

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:32.579
Because that's what it feels like, right?

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.614
It kind of feels like an attack.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:35.148
I don't know.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:35.448
I mean,

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.450
I think I get super charged by

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:40.587
the people I love and just having

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:43.523
an amazing family and friendships and,

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:44.524
you know,

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:45.425
now two kids

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.659
who are kind of looking up at

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:47.427
you expecting you

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:48.795
to have all the answers.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:51.130
And if it's put a fine point on

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.432
why we're doing all of this,

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:55.735
you know, and I think it's

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:57.971
I imagine them kind of

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.072
and they're only five,

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.340
so they're not quite on top of

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.475
current events. Yeah.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:03.876
And if you don't believe that,

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:04.677
I bet you they know

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.179
more than most people.

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:08.481
Well, actually,

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:08.915
my son

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:09.549
drew a

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:10.984
picture the other day of a prison,

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:12.986
and he was like, Putin should be in here.

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:15.722
And I was like, oh, my goodness.

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:16.522
Maybe I went a little

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:17.490
I didn't know anyone.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.891
I don't know what he overheard,

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:22.295
but I am working on Ukraine now.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:23.663
I you know,

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:25.898
but I do think about in a few years when

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.801
maybe five or more when they sort of

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.803
start to learn about some of these issues

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:31.471
that we're talking about

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.605
and what's happening in the world.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.741
And, you know, when they ask us,

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.242
what did you do about this?

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.745
What did you say about that?

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.346
You know, what will my answer be?

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.815
And I, I hope it will be a good one.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:44.984
I think it's important to tell all girls

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.519
that you can be whatever you want to be.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.254
You can be a mom

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:50.723
and a working mom or a working woman

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.158
and not a mom or mom

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.192
and stay home

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.762
like all of these choices are. Okay.

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:56.763
And guess what?

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.298
You can also get it wrong with your kids.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.132
So same thing.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:04:59.565
My kids

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.367
my daughter was five my oldest,

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.536
and she told her doll to lay down

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:04.971
because it had HIV aids

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.472
and she needed to take care of it.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:07.607
And I thought, oh, my God, I've

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:09.242
gone way too far on my work.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.778
No, prison drawings?

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:12.679
No.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:14.747
I have one question

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:16.115
that I'd like you all to answer

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:16.616
because I thought

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:18.251
this is a brilliant idea.

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.752
So the Girls Opportunity

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.487
Alliance asked girls

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:24.190
to write to their 25 year old self.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.592
And since we are so young,

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.996
I'm going to ask you to reverse that.

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:30.930
What would you

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.832
and I'll start here with you, Melinda,

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:36.803
what would you tell your 25 year old self

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:40.573
now that you've lived a life

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:42.709
I would say

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:45.111
life is even more beautiful ahead

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:46.713
than you realize.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.948
And I would say to my 25 year old self,

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:51.184
you knew in high school who you were

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:54.220
and you let go of some of that for

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.254
lots of reasons.

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.356
People,

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:59.125
situations, college people around you,

00:05:59.258 --> 00:06:00.493
you knew who you were

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:02.161
and once you learn to re

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.831
be the girl you were in high school

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:06.566
is when you grew into the full

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:08.668
woman that you could be. Boom

00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:10.503
Mrs.

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:13.272
Obama, that part

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:16.209
just simply

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:16.976
what I would tell

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:19.112
myself, you are good enough,

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:20.313
you are valued,

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:21.347
you are worthy,

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:24.083
your story matters, your voice matters.

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:24.851
You will do

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:26.252
the great things that you know

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:27.420
you can do.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.856
There was something that struck a chord.

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:31.891
It's like we all knew who we were

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:33.993
when we were little.

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.128
We knew our power.

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:37.263
Then it was just second guessed.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.600
So I would tell myself to follow

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.769
that instinct that

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:45.271
pay attention to that flame in you

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:48.441
because it is real and keep it fueled.

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:50.843
And don't let anybody try to blow it out

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:53.112
because you're going to need it.

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:54.180
Once you

00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:55.481
in.

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:57.183
It's so inspiring to hear Mrs.

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:59.619
Obama and Melinda Gates

00:06:59.619 --> 00:07:01.020
share about

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.121
what they would tell themselves

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:03.289
in their 25 years old.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:05.792
I think the best thing I would say is

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:07.560
if there's nothing,

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.695
if there's something good

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:12.031
that someone can be put to invest on

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:15.234
and has the best interest in this world

00:07:15.535 --> 00:07:16.936
is knowledge and

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:21.407
let's keep on encouraging our girls.

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:23.643
Keep on doin it.

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:25.411
Keep on believe in yourself.

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:27.213
Keep on. You'll get in there.

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:28.414
Keep on

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:30.950
Let's get her there.

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:34.754
No interest

00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:37.256
among them, what they said.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:40.026
I know it's hard being last on this one.

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:42.662
You know, I would say

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:46.065
define failure as not trying

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:47.467
because actually

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:48.768
going for things and falling

00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:50.269
flat on your face is fine.

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.671
It's a learning experience.

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:52.772
It makes you stronger.

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.707
But if you don't try

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:55.808
and if you don't actually

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:57.109
follow your dreams

00:07:57.109 --> 00:07:59.612
or even admit what they are

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:00.313
and go for it,

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:01.547
something that will stay with you.

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:04.150
So the idea is go for it.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:05.885
Get there and get others there

00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:08.221
because you do work all around the world.

00:08:08.254 --> 00:08:09.522
Where in the world

00:08:09.522 --> 00:08:11.257
are you most concerned about?

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:13.526
What is happening to girls and women

00:08:13.526 --> 00:08:14.160
right now?

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:17.864
Everywhere?

00:08:17.864 --> 00:08:20.566
It's unfortunately I mean, you know,

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:22.101
at the moment

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:24.270
I'm working on with our foundation

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.605
gathering evidence of crimes

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:26.105
being committed

00:08:26.105 --> 00:08:27.673
against women and girls,

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:29.208
among others in Ukraine.

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:31.611
You know, I've spent seven years

00:08:31.911 --> 00:08:33.312
working on cases

00:08:33.312 --> 00:08:34.514
where I represent

00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:37.083
women who were victims of

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:38.651
enslavement and sexual violence

00:08:38.651 --> 00:08:39.619
committed by ISIS.

00:08:39.619 --> 00:08:42.121
And that's women from Syria and Iraq.

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:44.090
We know one in three girls in the world

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:45.525
has suffered

00:08:45.525 --> 00:08:47.059
sexual or gender based violence.

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:48.160
That's a huge number.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.629
And the problem is

00:08:49.629 --> 00:08:50.830
it's going to keep happening

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.532
if we don't have accountability.

00:08:52.532 --> 00:08:54.300
So at our foundation,

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.067
we call what we do

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:56.869
waging justice, because,

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:57.236
you know,

00:08:57.236 --> 00:08:58.471
we cannot assume that

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:00.706
justice is just going to happen.

00:09:00.706 --> 00:09:02.441
You have to actually fight for it.

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:03.543
You have to make it happen.

00:09:03.543 --> 00:09:05.444
And, you know,

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:06.879
you can't even assume

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:07.813
that things are going to move

00:09:07.813 --> 00:09:08.714
in the right direction.

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:10.349
We are think backsliding.

00:09:10.349 --> 00:09:12.151
You know, ask a girl in Afghanistan

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:13.452
where the clocks have turned back.

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:16.656
20 years on her rights set against that.

00:09:16.656 --> 00:09:18.157
I do also see

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:18.991
through my work

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:21.160
the bravest people in the world

00:09:21.661 --> 00:09:23.596
being women and young girls

00:09:23.596 --> 00:09:25.698
who sometimes have suffered

00:09:25.698 --> 00:09:26.899
the worst crimes, you know,

00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:29.001
genocide and sexual enslavement.

00:09:29.402 --> 00:09:31.370
And they are the ones fighting back,

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:32.572
fighting for justice.

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:33.940
And I have to say

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:36.242
you know, today, watching on our screens

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:37.343
what's happening in

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:39.845
Iran with girls who've suffered,

00:09:39.979 --> 00:09:41.581
you know, the worst brutality,

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:43.082
but a protest movement

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:44.050
and you know,

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:45.685
being led by

00:09:45.685 --> 00:09:46.419
girls in school

00:09:46.419 --> 00:09:48.688
uniform who are facing off against

00:09:48.688 --> 00:09:49.422
a regime

00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:52.658
that is using force to torture and kill.

00:09:52.658 --> 00:09:53.793
And they're still determined

00:09:53.793 --> 00:09:54.760
because if

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.329
they're not the ones on the front lines,

00:09:56.329 --> 00:09:58.464
they they can't rely on others

00:09:58.464 --> 00:09:59.265
for change.

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:00.600
And I think that's incredible.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:02.835
And I think it also gives us perspective

00:10:02.835 --> 00:10:05.137
If girls like that can risk everything

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:06.572
to, you know,

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:07.273
just be free

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:08.708
to show their hair

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:11.310
and have just basic freedoms, then

00:10:11.711 --> 00:10:13.012
we can all do more,

00:10:13.012 --> 00:10:14.380
you know, from where we're sitting.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.916
And so I, I find that really inspiring.

